WEBVTT

00:40.874 --> 00:42.041
Here we go.

01:00.685 --> 01:02.729
What? What's wrong?!

01:04.856 --> 01:07.901
-Hajime! Yue!
-Calm yourselves!

01:07.984 --> 01:09.944
Kaori! Pull yourself together!

01:10.862 --> 01:13.114
Yeah! I'll treat them right away!

03:03.516 --> 03:08.021
-What are you doing, Yue?
-A wake-up kiss.

03:08.688 --> 03:12.483
I got dragged into this room
after I collapsed?

03:12.567 --> 03:14.193
What about the others?

03:14.944 --> 03:16.070
I'm sorry.

03:16.154 --> 03:19.032
I don't know, since I just woke up.

03:19.115 --> 03:21.242
How long have you been conscious?

03:22.535 --> 03:23.828
About ten minutes?

03:23.912 --> 03:27.248
And you've been like this the whole time?

03:28.291 --> 03:30.293
When I woke up, you were there.

03:31.711 --> 03:36.257
Yue. I think it'll take some time
before I wake up.

03:37.467 --> 03:40.178
I'll let Shea and the rest
know after you're awake.

03:43.139 --> 03:45.516
Hey, you're awake!

03:45.600 --> 03:49.229
Hajime. Yue. What are you two doing? Well?

03:51.981 --> 03:53.358
Come back in two hours.

03:53.441 --> 03:54.817
Are you stupid?!

03:54.901 --> 03:56.569
Not a chance in hell!

03:57.487 --> 04:00.406
H-Have a little prudence, you two!

04:02.533 --> 04:03.409
Whoa there.

04:04.160 --> 04:06.162
What the heck happened?

04:07.163 --> 04:09.958
I can pretty much guess.

04:12.085 --> 04:12.919
Abe!

04:14.295 --> 04:16.339
Punishment for
looking at Yue for a second.

04:16.923 --> 04:18.383
That's way too unreasonable!

04:19.342 --> 04:20.760
Are you jealous?

04:21.803 --> 04:23.304
How cute, Hajime.

04:23.388 --> 04:27.350
Sheesh! You two haven't learned anything!

04:27.433 --> 04:30.228
Do you know how worried we were?!

04:30.311 --> 04:32.605
Shea's right.

04:33.273 --> 04:35.692
We really were worried.

04:35.775 --> 04:36.901
That's right.

04:36.985 --> 04:39.279
You should have let us know you were fine.

04:39.362 --> 04:43.157
Ah, well, I'm really sorry.

04:43.241 --> 04:47.954
Yue kissed me when I woke up,
so I lost all reason…

04:48.037 --> 04:50.832
Yeah, it's all because
Yue is too adorable.

04:51.833 --> 04:53.001
I'm sorry.

04:53.084 --> 04:55.586
I should have let you know right away.

04:55.670 --> 05:00.174
Seeing Hajime defenseless
next to me made me lose control.

05:00.258 --> 05:02.510
It's all because Hajime's too handsome.

05:04.887 --> 05:08.057
You two really haven't learned a thing.

05:08.975 --> 05:10.268
That's enough.

05:10.351 --> 05:13.021
Any more and it'll tire me out mentally.

05:13.104 --> 05:17.775
Seeing them after realizing my own
feelings really hurts in many ways.

05:17.859 --> 05:21.571
Oh! Master and Yue are both okay.

05:21.654 --> 05:23.406
What a relief.

05:23.489 --> 05:25.325
Tio, my apologies.

05:25.408 --> 05:28.661
-I forgot to let you know.
-It's fine.

05:28.745 --> 05:34.125
I bet Master and Yue woke up
and were getting freaky.

05:34.208 --> 05:35.626
You really know them well…

05:35.710 --> 05:38.421
Yes, but of course.

05:38.504 --> 05:42.050
I'd do the same thing if I were Yue.

05:42.133 --> 05:47.221
Then Master would scornfully look down
at my aroused self, and do this and that…

05:47.305 --> 05:51.142
Anyway.
What exactly happened to the two of you?

05:51.809 --> 05:56.898
It must have been something fierce to
make you scream in anguish and pass out.

05:56.981 --> 05:58.649
That's right.

05:58.733 --> 06:03.946
To put it simply, it's like our minds
and psyches were forced to overheat.

06:04.030 --> 06:05.239
I see.

06:05.323 --> 06:08.868
A cognitive load that
not even you two can withstand…

06:08.951 --> 06:11.746
You two must have learned
the particulars of concept magic.

06:11.829 --> 06:14.040
Yeah. Good job, Tio.

06:14.123 --> 06:16.042
You may be a pervert, but you're sharp.

06:16.125 --> 06:19.212
Magic that manifests concepts themselves.

06:19.295 --> 06:21.923
Once you've obtained it,
we can return to Japan, right?

06:22.006 --> 06:23.424
No, not yet.

06:24.050 --> 06:28.513
The knowledge we gained is
more like prerequisite knowledge.

06:28.596 --> 06:29.972
Prerequisite knowledge?

06:30.056 --> 06:31.516
Yeah.

06:31.599 --> 06:34.477
The absolute requirement
for mastering concept magic

06:34.560 --> 06:38.773
is complete understanding
of all ancient magic.

06:40.108 --> 06:42.276
<i>Take creation magic.</i>

06:42.360 --> 06:45.571
<i>Its essence is not the power</i>
<i>to imbue minerals with magic,</i>

06:45.655 --> 06:48.658
<i>but rather to tamper with</i>
<i>inorganic materials.</i>

06:49.158 --> 06:53.830
<i>Gravity magic is tampering with</i>
<i>the energy of heavenly bodies.</i>

06:54.497 --> 06:58.000
<i>Spatial magic is tampering</i>
<i>with boundaries.</i>

06:58.835 --> 07:02.547
<i>Regeneration magic is tampering with time.</i>

07:03.214 --> 07:08.469
<i>Spirit magic is tampering with</i>
<i>immaterial aspects of living things.</i>

07:08.553 --> 07:12.473
<i>Evolution magic is</i>
<i>tampering with information.</i>

07:13.141 --> 07:16.185
<i>And if you had to define</i>
<i>metamorphosis magic,</i>

07:16.269 --> 07:18.938
<i>it's tampering with organic materials.</i>

07:19.021 --> 07:22.733
Yeah.
Understanding all that is so profound,

07:22.817 --> 07:25.695
that unless you've cleared all the trials,

07:25.778 --> 07:28.865
your mind and body would
break down from the unbearable load.

07:28.948 --> 07:33.786
From what you say,
it sounds extremely difficult.

07:33.870 --> 07:36.038
It's true that it's difficult.

07:36.622 --> 07:39.917
Not to mention that the most important
ingredient for turning concepts into magic

07:40.001 --> 07:42.086
is extreme willpower.

07:42.170 --> 07:45.006
Yeah. With Hajime's creation magic,

07:45.089 --> 07:48.134
we need to imbue an item
with magic, much like the compass.

07:48.217 --> 07:49.552
That's right.

07:49.635 --> 07:53.389
Yue's powers of control
over magic, and my alchemy.

07:53.473 --> 07:54.807
In total sync,

07:54.891 --> 07:59.061
we need to create an artifact
imbued with the concept to cross worlds.

07:59.145 --> 08:00.938
Don't tell me it's impossible.

08:01.022 --> 08:02.315
Of course not.

08:02.398 --> 08:05.067
We'll succeed, no matter what it takes.

08:05.151 --> 08:06.986
That's the reason
we've struggled all this time.

08:09.447 --> 08:11.949
-Will you attempt it right away?
-Yeah.

08:12.450 --> 08:14.911
I managed to mentally
sort it all out as I explained it.

08:14.994 --> 08:16.704
Nothing to do but test it out.

08:16.787 --> 08:18.331
Um, Nagumo.

08:18.414 --> 08:20.625
If it's going to take some time,

08:20.708 --> 08:25.505
I think I should go off and take care
of my other goal.

08:25.588 --> 08:28.299
No, it shouldn't take that long.

08:28.382 --> 08:29.509
I see.

08:29.592 --> 08:32.345
In that case, I'll get some rest.

08:32.428 --> 08:35.014
I want to practice using
metamorphosis magic,

08:35.097 --> 08:37.683
so I'll head into demon
territory after that.

08:37.767 --> 08:40.228
Um, what about Shizu-Shizu and the others?

08:40.311 --> 08:43.439
Of course I'll go with you.

08:43.523 --> 08:45.066
Me too.

08:46.359 --> 08:48.528
Thanks, you two.

08:48.611 --> 08:51.822
N-Now all we need is Koki.

08:52.865 --> 08:55.368
Oh yeah, where did he go?

08:56.953 --> 08:58.579
Finally noticed, huh?

08:59.121 --> 09:01.249
Koki's still asleep in another room.

09:01.916 --> 09:04.043
It'll be some time before he comes to.

09:04.126 --> 09:06.879
Well, I don't care about him.

09:06.963 --> 09:09.632
We'll be holing up in that room
with the magic circle.

09:09.715 --> 09:12.969
Even if Amanogawa wakes up,
don't let him interfere.

09:13.761 --> 09:16.430
You're making the tools
we need to get home.

09:16.514 --> 09:18.015
I'm sure he wouldn't do that.

09:18.099 --> 09:20.101
I can only hope so.

09:20.184 --> 09:21.561
Well, just to be safe.

09:21.644 --> 09:24.105
Leave it to me, Hajime!

09:24.188 --> 09:26.857
I won't let anyone get in your way!

09:28.192 --> 09:29.944
Yeah. Thanks, Shea.

09:30.027 --> 09:32.196
I can rest assured with Shea here.

09:33.698 --> 09:35.283
You think it'll be okay?

09:35.366 --> 09:39.662
Suzu, what's "it" referring to here?

09:40.705 --> 09:41.956
I guess everything.

09:42.039 --> 09:46.335
Like, will Nagumo end up collapsing again?

09:46.419 --> 09:49.380
And can we really go back to Japan?

09:49.463 --> 09:52.091
Will Koki be okay?

09:52.592 --> 09:55.136
And what about when we
head into demon territory?

09:55.219 --> 09:57.096
It'll be fine.

09:57.179 --> 10:02.393
No matter the obstacle, Hajime
always overcomes it in the end,

10:02.476 --> 10:05.062
so I'm sure he can make
the impossible possible.

10:05.146 --> 10:06.647
Kaorin…

10:06.731 --> 10:11.611
As for Koki, he's the only one
who can change himself.

10:11.694 --> 10:13.738
And as for Eri…

10:15.114 --> 10:18.200
For now, let's just
think about charging in!

10:18.284 --> 10:21.912
That's all we can do, and thinking
about it will only tire you out.

10:23.080 --> 10:25.791
You're so manly, Kaorin!

10:25.875 --> 10:28.919
Hajime's really rubbed off on you.

10:29.003 --> 10:30.463
That's not true, Suzu.

10:30.546 --> 10:34.925
Kaori's always been the type to charge in
once she's made up her mind.

10:35.009 --> 10:38.804
Kaori's decisions end with her
charging in 90 percent of the time.

10:38.888 --> 10:41.599
You and Suzu are both so mean!

10:41.682 --> 10:45.019
You're making me sound like
I'm the same as Ryutaro!

10:45.102 --> 10:46.520
Hey, Kaori.

10:46.604 --> 10:49.815
Why would it be mean
to say you're the same as me?

10:49.899 --> 10:52.193
Do you realize you're
casually insulting me?

10:52.860 --> 10:56.864
Anyway, I'll be with
you when you go see Eri,

10:56.947 --> 10:59.742
and in the worst case,
I can dismantle everything around us,

10:59.825 --> 11:02.495
so we can run away amidst the chaos.

11:02.578 --> 11:06.666
U-Um, you're coming with us, Kaorin?

11:06.749 --> 11:08.209
Of course I am.

11:08.292 --> 11:10.378
I can't let you go off by yourself,

11:10.461 --> 11:12.880
and after all this,
I want all of us to go back together.

11:12.963 --> 11:14.715
Thanks!

11:15.341 --> 11:18.552
With Kaori and Shizuku,
I'm sure you'll be fine.

11:19.804 --> 11:25.184
I should visit home
before we go to Master's world, too.

11:25.267 --> 11:27.395
Since I left the village with a mission.

11:27.478 --> 11:29.647
Oh, that's right.

11:29.730 --> 11:32.983
You received secret
orders from your family.

11:33.067 --> 11:34.527
Shea.

11:34.610 --> 11:37.530
You want to see Cam and the others
again as well, don't you?

11:37.613 --> 11:38.864
That's true.

11:39.949 --> 11:43.077
Oh, looks like you're awake.

11:43.160 --> 11:46.205
-How are you feeling?
-I feel fine.

11:46.288 --> 11:48.707
Sorry to make you worry.

11:48.791 --> 11:52.420
It's a little late for that.
I'm just glad you're okay.

11:52.503 --> 11:55.297
Yeah, I'm happy to see you back in action.

11:55.381 --> 11:57.049
What a relief!

12:03.305 --> 12:08.018
Hajime's not here, since he's
secluded himself in another room.

12:08.102 --> 12:09.395
I see.

12:10.229 --> 12:14.358
After all the trouble I caused,
I thought I should apologize.

12:15.067 --> 12:17.820
Sounds like you're back
to your senses now.

12:17.903 --> 12:23.409
Or do you still think Nagumo
has brainwashed all of us?

12:24.702 --> 12:26.787
Koki, look me in the eye.

12:29.290 --> 12:32.835
No, I don't think that anymore.

12:32.918 --> 12:35.588
Something was really
wrong with me back then.

12:37.506 --> 12:38.507
I see.

12:39.467 --> 12:42.636
So everyone else obtained ancient magic.

12:43.304 --> 12:44.180
Koki.

12:44.930 --> 12:48.184
I'm in love with Nagumo now.

12:49.810 --> 12:52.646
I want him to see me as a woman.

12:53.272 --> 12:57.902
Does that mean
you'll go with Nagumo, then?

12:57.985 --> 13:00.738
Nagumo already has
a favorite, and Kaori as well.

13:01.405 --> 13:03.449
I think you should reconsider it.

13:03.532 --> 13:07.536
-I'm saying this for your own good.
-I wasn't asking you for your opinion.

13:08.204 --> 13:10.164
I just wanted to let you know.

13:10.247 --> 13:11.832
As your childhood friend.

13:17.755 --> 13:19.465
You're all on his side, huh?

13:19.548 --> 13:23.636
Even though he'll kill and abandon
people with no hesitation.

13:23.719 --> 13:24.762
Koki!

13:26.514 --> 13:31.602
If I knew this would happen, I should
have fallen off that bridge instead…

13:36.815 --> 13:40.152
I consider you my
precious childhood friend.

13:40.903 --> 13:44.073
So… please…

13:45.282 --> 13:46.492
Kaori…

13:49.453 --> 13:51.413
Hajime! Yue!

14:09.640 --> 14:12.434
Sh-Shea! What's going on?

14:12.518 --> 14:13.978
I'm not sure.

14:14.061 --> 14:17.940
But for now, it looks like
the two of them are fine.

14:18.023 --> 14:20.234
If they're safe, we should leave.

14:20.317 --> 14:21.902
Indeed.

14:21.986 --> 14:24.738
If they fail because of us…

14:24.822 --> 14:27.741
We'll have to be punished!

14:27.825 --> 14:31.161
Don't sound so happy about it, Tio.

14:41.964 --> 14:42.923
Koki.

14:53.642 --> 14:55.978
That kind of looks like Orcus.

14:56.061 --> 14:57.646
That's true.

14:57.730 --> 15:03.235
The Great Orcus Labyrinth is a
giant cave lit by green glowing stones.

15:03.903 --> 15:07.114
This emotion… Is it unease?

15:07.197 --> 15:08.866
And urgency.

15:08.949 --> 15:10.826
I sense fear as well.

15:10.910 --> 15:13.871
What we're seeing is a memory.

15:27.927 --> 15:29.261
Hajime!

15:30.012 --> 15:31.430
Oh no!

15:34.016 --> 15:36.727
<i>Somebody help me…</i>

15:38.103 --> 15:41.941
<i>What did I ever do to deserve this?</i>

15:43.651 --> 15:47.404
<i>Why? Why? Why?</i>

15:48.781 --> 15:50.699
<i>What I wish for…</i>

15:51.408 --> 15:53.911
<i>Everything that stands in the way of that…</i>

15:54.662 --> 15:57.665
<i>I… I…</i>

16:00.459 --> 16:01.418
<i>I want to go home…</i>

16:06.256 --> 16:08.050
<i>I want to go home.</i>

16:10.636 --> 16:12.596
<i>I want to go home!</i>

16:16.600 --> 16:17.768
<i>I'll go home.</i>

16:18.602 --> 16:21.605
<i>I'll make sure I survive</i>
<i>and return to my homeland!</i>

16:30.406 --> 16:32.700
Go home, huh?

16:35.369 --> 16:36.787
Is that…

16:37.538 --> 16:39.707
A key?

16:41.291 --> 16:44.044
Open the door to the place of your wishes.

17:00.394 --> 17:02.980
Hajime! Yue! Are you okay?!

17:05.482 --> 17:07.651
Kaori, how are they?!

17:12.072 --> 17:13.949
Yeah, they're fine.

17:14.033 --> 17:16.035
They've just passed out.

17:16.118 --> 17:19.163
Due to mana exhaustion, it seems.

17:32.801 --> 17:34.178
How'd it go?

17:35.554 --> 17:36.930
Where's the artifact?

17:37.681 --> 17:40.893
I've given you some of
my mana, so you'll be fine.

17:40.976 --> 17:44.271
Although I can't say
anything about the artifact.

17:44.354 --> 17:45.564
I see.

17:45.647 --> 17:47.232
Thanks, Kaori.

17:47.316 --> 17:52.279
I didn't have a good feel for it,
so I used all the power I had.

17:54.281 --> 17:55.949
Can we fine-tune it for next time?

17:56.033 --> 17:58.077
Yeah, it's okay.

17:58.160 --> 18:00.370
I've gotten the hang of it now.

18:00.454 --> 18:05.209
The problem is manifesting enough
willpower to materialize the concept.

18:06.710 --> 18:08.796
It turned out real nice.

18:08.879 --> 18:10.672
I can feel great power from it.

18:10.756 --> 18:13.175
It feels similar to the
Everguiding Compass.

18:14.468 --> 18:17.096
-Thanks, Yue.
-Yeah!

18:21.225 --> 18:23.477
Let's try this out.

18:42.996 --> 18:44.665
It's a success!

18:46.083 --> 18:48.418
We've found a way to go back home!

18:48.502 --> 18:51.213
-Yay!
-Awesome!

19:02.182 --> 19:06.395
Now we just need an artifact to prevent us
from being summoned back here.

19:06.478 --> 19:07.312
Yeah.

19:07.396 --> 19:12.192
It'd be nice to get it done while we
pick up Myu, or while Tio returns home.

19:12.734 --> 19:14.444
But I can't say for sure.

19:15.112 --> 19:20.951
For now, we'll work on
creating an anti-summoning artifact,

19:21.034 --> 19:23.370
while we start heading to pick Myu up.

19:23.453 --> 19:26.498
In that case,
we'll head into demon territory.

19:27.082 --> 19:29.793
We finally got our hands on ancient magic,

19:29.877 --> 19:33.881
so it'd be nice to have some
powerful monsters under our control…

19:34.464 --> 19:35.382
Taniguchi.

19:37.718 --> 19:42.181
That gate key is connected
to the gate hole I set up in Verbergen.

19:42.264 --> 19:44.850
Why don't you try subjugating
some monsters from the Sea of Trees?

19:44.933 --> 19:45.851
I see.

19:46.518 --> 19:49.521
There's a lot of monsters there
skilled at manipulating their aura.

19:50.230 --> 19:53.692
If you subdue them and buff their
strength, they should come in quite handy.

19:53.775 --> 19:55.652
Yeah, I'll give it a shot.

19:55.736 --> 19:57.571
Thanks, Nagumo.

19:57.654 --> 20:00.616
Suzu, I'll be going with you.

20:00.699 --> 20:05.913
Yue and I will get some rest
until our mana's fully topped off.

20:05.996 --> 20:06.997
Yeah.

20:16.548 --> 20:19.635
So why are you staying behind?

20:19.718 --> 20:21.011
Especially you, Shea.

20:21.094 --> 20:25.724
Yeah. I thought you'd return to Verbergen
with Kaori and the rest.

20:25.807 --> 20:31.271
I wanted to see if I could master my
dragon form with metamorphosis magic.

20:31.355 --> 20:34.233
I, um…

20:34.942 --> 20:38.695
<i>don't like dealing with</i>
<i>the elder's granddaughter…</i>

20:38.779 --> 20:41.573
Ah, that princess?

20:46.787 --> 20:50.207
Now then, I guess we should get going.

20:54.127 --> 20:55.712
Oh, that's right.

20:56.588 --> 20:58.382
Take this, Hajime.

20:59.049 --> 21:00.968
The clear symbol?

21:01.051 --> 21:02.678
I completely forgot.

21:34.376 --> 21:37.963
Now that's a shortcut
right out of a fantasy.

21:38.046 --> 21:39.298
A reward for us?

21:50.767 --> 21:55.272
Looks like it's nice enough to take us
to the border of the Schnee Snow Fields.

21:55.355 --> 21:58.692
Going by the sun's position,
it's headed northwest.

21:59.443 --> 22:01.987
The demon territory is right there.

22:02.070 --> 22:03.947
I'm done running away.

22:04.031 --> 22:05.907
I'll go talk with Eri!

22:06.700 --> 22:08.577
We need to bring her back quickly.

22:09.161 --> 22:11.747
And go pick up everyone
else from class, too.

22:11.830 --> 22:15.125
Yeah. Let's all go back home together.

22:15.792 --> 22:17.044
That's right.

22:17.127 --> 22:19.838
I can't wait to return home.

22:20.672 --> 22:22.632
I'm sure they'll all be surprised.

22:22.716 --> 22:24.051
I bet.

22:24.134 --> 22:27.345
Their own kind,
coming back home as a pervert.

22:28.346 --> 22:29.431
Hajime.

22:31.850 --> 22:34.770
I can't wait to meet your family.

22:38.190 --> 22:40.650
Yeah. It won't be long.

24:37.225 --> 24:39.477
Bring it on, Irregular!
